###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All errors (force RMSEs, Fig. 1; 2- and 4-body curve RMSEs, Fig. 4; RDF errors; data-size and noise studies, Figs. 6-8) are figure-only. Models trained on Liquid 1 and Cluster (five splits each) are not encoded as separate runs.
# - The number of points on the 4-body curve and the size of the RDF system are not stated, so no per-atom times are derived. The MACE RDF runs used a GPU while ACE and HDNNP used 8 CPU cores.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/sandberg2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
